<title>USA: Carolina 767 MW nuke seen on line Thursday.</title>
<headline>Carolina 767 MW nuke seen on line Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carolina Power &amp; Light Co's 767 megawatt Brunswick nuclear power unit 1 is set to synchronize to the electricity grid on Thursday after restarting this week, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;It should be synched to the grid tomorrow,&quot; company spokesman Mac Harris said Wednesday, adding it will take several more days before the unit is up to full production.</p>
<p>The Southport, N.C., unit is returning from a scheduled maintenance and refueling outage which began Oct 5.</p>
<p>--Chris Reese, New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
